# TLS front door: Caddy terminates HTTPS for the DuckDNS hostname with
# automatic Let's Encrypt certificates. The proxy target is IMPORTED from a
# separate one-line file (upstream.caddy, written by the deploy):
#   reverse_proxy edg_client_blue:80    # or edg_client_green:80
# A release flips the upstream by rewriting that file and running a graceful
# `docker exec edg_caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile` — no
# TLS blip, in-flight requests drain.
expressdevelopersguide.duckdns.org {
    import /etc/caddy/upstream.caddy
}
